cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this software when using the patient-level pipeline, and also
  cite the original TCGA study and the Infinium probe-annotation resource
  described in the data provenance documentation.
type: software
title: "HNSC methylation: a reproducible Python pipeline"
authors:
  - family-names: Sinkala
    given-names: Musalula
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Python functions and a Jupyter notebook for cohort preparation,
  annotation-based probe filtering, differential methylation,
  cross-validated classification, matched methylation-expression
  association, survival modelling, robustness checks and figure generation
  in TCGA HNSC. AFR and EUR denote the recorded clinical race categories
  Black or African American and White; they are not inferred genetic ancestry.
keywords:
  - DNA methylation
  - head and neck squamous cell carcinoma
  - TCGA
  - reproducible research
  - epigenetics

